  m_text: 'Title IX Enacted in the United States of America - 1972



    Pictured
    here is one of the many marches that called for female equality. The many marches
    and persistence of the determined women led to the signing of Title IX, which
    is a civil rights law that prohibits sex-based discrimination in education and
    activities that received federal assistance. This pushed women more into athletics
    in schools due to them receiving equal athletic opportunities and treatment.'
