  m_text: 'Alice Milliat



    Pictured here is Alice Milliat, the creator of the
    Women''s Olympics of 1922. Due to the ban of female athletes in the Olympics,
    Alice took matters into her own hands and created her own Women''s Olympics to
    put women in the spotlight. Her Olympics received national recognition being
    held in Paris and with only female competitors.'
