  m_text: 'First Olympic Women''s Marathon - 1984



    Pictured here are the female
    competitors in the first Olympic marathon trials ran in Olympia, Washington.
    These women overcame the stigma that "women can''t run long distance," and especially
    Joan Benoit who held the record for fastest time for an American woman to run
    the marathon for 32 years.'
