      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'First Women''s Olympiad - 1922



    Pictured here are two female competitors
    that competed in the first Women''s Olympics that was organized by Alice Milliat.
    Due to the male-dominated Olympics, Alice created her own Women''s Olympics in
    Paris to show that women are just as competitive and capable as men. The turnout
    to the Women''s Olympics were 77 athletes and an audience of 20,000.'
