  m_text: 'Women''s World Cup Final - 1991



    Pictured here is the US team that
    claimed the first Women''s World Cup, defeating Norway in the World Cup Championship
    played in China''s Tianhe Stadium. At the time FIFA had strong opinions about
    a Women''s World Cup, so they renamed it World Championship for Women''s Football
    and tried to move it out of western eyes. However, once the news of the US team''s
    success spread, FIFA finally moved the women''s games back to view and now recognize
    the Women''s World Cup.'
